                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Can you survive 2 minutes?\n\nIt's a very simple but difficult game. Similar to Asteroids, except you're an immobile circle in the center of the screen that can only rotate 360 degrees but not move otherwise. Enemies (triangles of varying sizes) come directly at you from all directions. Smaller enemies take fewer shots to kill than larger ones. \n\nArrow keys rotate. Spacebar fires your main weapon. Hold spacebar for a larger shot that does more damage. Each shot you take depletes the shot power bar. \n\nPress Q to fire heat-seeking missiles, of which you have a limited supply, so use them only in emergencies. The main missle will break off into a series of smaller missiles after striking its first target.\n\nYour shield deflects enemy shots back at them, but does not hold up for long. It will replenish itself occasionally. \n\nDefeating bosses (giant triangles) will drop powerups that you can use to levl up your shot power, regain health, etc.\n\nThere is an element of randomness which can make it frustrating, but also leads to the urge to try it one more time. \n\nI know I can beat my high score!",
